{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: members_can_write (Layer-2, app-owned; spec §12.2).
  Permits any AUTHENTICATED principal to perform a write. Every bearer is bound to
  a real member, so an authenticated caller is a member. Named separately from
  public_read so write access is a distinct, visible decision in review. Fail-closed
  by construction (the engine denies if this partial is missing or errors).
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign r = '{}' | parse_json
  hash_assign r['allow'] = true
  hash_assign r['reason'] = 'member'
  return r
%}
